      "value": "@{60bbf9cb4701af68ae65c329|full_name} I agree there would inevitably be some reuploads. However, that already happens with malicious and raid avatars regardless. If a new Avatar ID appears, groups could simply add that ID to their blocklist as well.\n\nThe goal istn to make it impossible for someone to ever reupload a malicious avatar, but to give communities a proactive tool against known malicious avatars. Over time, groups could build up a database of IDs they've encountered instead of having to deal with the exact same avatars repeatedly.\n\nReuploading also adds another step for the person causing trouble, while blocking a newly discovered ID would take moderators only a few seconds and it would be applied to anyone using that in the future once more.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
